Upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp 479a52779 (#30737, "ggml-cpu : compute f32 gelu_quick and geglu_quick without the fp16 table"), MIT.
F32 gelu_quick / geglu_quick (the CLIP text encoders: SD1.x, SDXL, FLUX.1 CLIP-L) went through a 64K-entry
fp16 lookup table, rounding the input to fp16 first. They now compute x / (1 + exp(-1.702 x)) in f32 with the
existing SIMD expf (AVX512 / AVX2 / SSE2 / SVE / NEON / RVV); the fp16 and bf16 paths are unchanged.
Not bit-identical to the table (more accurate). The VXE branch is dropped (this ggml has no VXE expf).
Includes the upstream test-gelu-quick (F32 kernels vs a double-precision reference) and test-backend-ops cases.

